<section id="capabilities" class="capabilities wrap" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
  <div class="section-kicker mono"><span>04 / MADE FOR THE IN-BETWEEN</span><span>THE PRODUCT VISION</span></div>
  <div class="capabilities-heading"><h2 id="capabilities-title" data-reveal>Keep the feeling.<br /><em>Lose the guesswork.</em></h2><p>A concept for the conversations between<br />the first idea and the final sound.</p></div>
  <article class="capability-row"><div class="capability-copy"><span class="mono">01 / SPATIAL NOTES</span><h3>Put a pin<br />in the feeling.</h3><p>Attach feedback to a position in the scene. “Here” becomes a shared reference, with the context to make it useful.</p></div><div class="note-illustration" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a spatial note connected to a sound source"><div class="note-rings"></div><span class="note-pin">+</span><div class="spatial-note"><span class="mono">SCENE NOTE / 01</span><p>Let this arrive from<br />just beyond the doorway.</p><span class="note-meta mono">SIGNAL · REAR RIGHT</span></div><span class="illustration-label mono">FEEDBACK, WITH A SENSE OF DIRECTION.</span></div></article>
  <article class="capability-row reverse"><div class="capability-copy"><span class="mono">02 / CONTEXTUAL REVIEW</span><h3>One scene.<br />A shared perspective.</h3><p>Keep the source, its surroundings, and the conversation in the same frame. Review the intention behind a placement.</p></div><div class="review-illustration" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a focused source with contextual feedback"><div class="review-orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="review-orbit orbit-two"></div><span class="review-point">02</span><div class="review-comment"><span class="mono">FOCUS / VOICE</span><p>Closer feels more intimate.</p></div><div class="context-line mono"><span>ENVIRONMENT</span><i></i><span>INTENTION</span></div></div></article>
  <article class="capability-row"><div class="capability-copy"><span class="mono">03 / SCENE EVOLUTION</span><h3>Make room<br />for what’s next.</h3><p>Trace how a scene could evolve, with previous positions as a reference. A clearer way to talk about what changed, and why.</p></div><div class="evolution-illustration" role="img" aria-label="Illustration comparing three revisions of a source position"><div class="revision-grid">{[1,2,3].map((n)=><div class="revision"><span class="mono">0{n}</span><div class="revision-scene"><i style={`left:${25+n*15}%;top:${60-n*10}%`}></i></div><span class="mono">{['FIRST THOUGHT','A LITTLE CLOSER','NEW PERSPECTIVE'][n-1]}</span></div>)}</div><div class="evolution-track"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="illustration-label mono">EVERY ITERATION LEAVES A TRACE.</span></div></article>
  <p class="concept-note mono">THESE ARE PRODUCT CONCEPTS, ILLUSTRATED — NOT LIVE COLLABORATION TOOLS.</p>
</section>
